1950..2024 Comment "/// A path at every loop whose inverse arm drops its rest\'s path: each arm"
2025..2106 Comment "/// checks at its letter, but at `loop ∷ back(loop) ∷ q` the loop arm carries"
2107..2178 Comment "/// the inverse arm\'s reflexivity to `Path.here(loop ∷ back(loop) ∷"
2179..2196 Comment "/// q)`, which is"
2197..2272 Comment "/// not the path at `q` the cancellation\'s right side reads. Read as a set,"
2273..2341 Comment "/// the loops would identify the two; the words are not read as one."
